            <ArticleTitle>True and pseudo aneurysms of coronary arteries in a patient with Behçet's disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>465-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 33-year-old man with a 9-year history of Behçet's disease was hospitalized with a giant pseudo aneurysm of left anterior descending and true aneurysm of right coronary artery. This unusual vascular complication of Behçet's disease treated successfully is presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
